      "math_academy_id": "q-224529",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.26)$ given below, compute $P(3<X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1642\\,$ | $\\,0.5104\\,$ | $\\,0.8144\\,$ | $\\,0.9569\\,$ | $\\,0.9944\\,$ | $\\,0.9997\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(3<X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\})+P(X\\in \\{4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3)+P(3<X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(3)+P(3<X\\le 5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X\\le 5) & =F(5)-F(3) \\\\  & =0.9997-0.9569 \\\\  & =0.0428.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
